{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Ya'akov blessed Pharaoh.</b> He blessed him with wealth and the exaltation of his kingship, for so is the way of the elders and the pious when they come before kings — to bless them, in the manner of what is written concerning David (I Kings 1:31): ״יחי אדני המלך דוד״. And Scripture mentions a second time, ״ויברך יעקב את פרעה ויצא מלפני פרעה״ — for when he went out from before him he turned back and blessed him. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: he blessed him that the Nile should rise to meet him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:50.956164283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}